[11.015, "o", "\r\n"]
[11.031, "o", "  \u001b[35m\u2261  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;35mPlan         \u001b[0m1. Open **durations.py** and review the `_UNITS` dictionary \u2013 it      \r\n                  currently maps `\"m\"` to\u202f1 and `\"s\"` to\u202f60, which is inverted.         \r\n                  2. Update `_UNITS` to use correct second values: `{\"h\": 3600, \"m\": 60,\r\n                  \"s\": 1}`.                                                             \r\n                  3. Verify that the regular expression `_TOKEN =                       \r\n                  re.compile(r\"(\\d+)([hms])\")` correctly captures numbers and unit      \r\n                  letters for the test strings.                                         \r\n                  4. Run the test suite (`pytest tests/test_durations.py`) to confirm   \r\n                  `test_hours` and `test_minutes` now pass.                             \r\n                  5. If any other duration tests exist, ensure they also succeed after  \r\n                  the unit fix.                                                         \r\n"]
